From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CEB-GNRD board layer <bmc@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: update progress, BIOS flash region selection

Progress: a bar under the update form shows the upload percentage, then the
PercentComplete of the Redfish update task that bmcweb returns, polled every
2 s.  The package MANIFEST tells a BIOS update from a BMC update.  For the BIOS
the step is named from the progress value that the board's bios-update.sh
reports (waiting for the server to be off, switching the flash, reading,
erasing, writing, verifying, returning the flash, force-off pulse, power-on),
and the page reports success or the step that failed.  A BMC update ends
with a time based bar while the BMC reboots and writes its flash; the page
checks every 5 s whether the BMC answers again and then reloads itself (the
login page appears when the session did not survive the update).

Regions: for a BIOS package the page lists the regions of the board's fixed
BIOS flash layout as check boxes.  nac0/nac1 (settings and MAC addresses of
the CPU's integrated network controller) are not selected by default and can
only be selected after confirming a warning.  The selection is added to the
package as bios-regions.txt, which bios-update.sh uses to write only those
regions.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD board-specific update flow]
